Rule: an4-171-instigates-deeds — 2 change(s), 2 file(s)

--- sujato/sutta/an/an4/an4.171_translation-en-sujato.json
+++ sujato/sutta/an/an4/an4.171_translation-en-sujato.json
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@ an4.171:2.1
 PLI: Sāmaṁ vā taṁ, bhikkhave, kāyasaṅkhāraṁ abhisaṅkharoti, yaṁpaccayāssa taṁ uppajjati ajjhattaṁ sukhadukkhaṁ. 
-By oneself one instigates the action formation that gives rise to bodily, verbal, and mental action, conditioned by which that pleasure and pain arise in oneself. 
+By oneself one instigates the action formation that gives rise to bodily, verbal, and mental deeds, conditioned by which that pleasure and pain arise in oneself. 
